From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:36:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 535/535] [MoE] A lease prepared for the caller's output holds
 no output buffer

Since the layer's output is a tensor of its own, which the experts write in
place (output_alias), the arena's output buffer was leased and never used:
buffer 0 of the routed lease still held M_full x K of the output dtype (for
DeepSeek V4.1's TileLang experts, whose workspace13 is empty, that is all it
held: 10 KiB a row). The fresh output came on top of it.

_allocate_buffers takes the caller's output shape and leases no output buffer
when it is the experts' output and they write a matching alias (not on ROCm
without aiter, which copies from its own buffer); prepare_workspace passes
hidden_states' shape, and the per-call lease the alias's. A lease without an
output buffer refuses a call without a matching output. Outputs are unchanged:
the experts wrote the caller's tensor before and still do.

Tests: the lease's size with and without the output, the cases that keep the
buffer, the experts writing the caller's output into a lease without one; the
FlashInfer NVFP4 workspace tests assert the new contract (they still asserted
the output was workspace[2]).
